              "eyebrow": "Festival team security lab",
              "prompt": "Handle a fresh unknown-session case using the stated initial-response sequence.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">New case: a login alert and an unknown download arrive while the account owner is in class. The teacher is available. Follow the exerciseâ€™s initial-response sequence without contacting suspected users or deleting records.</p><div class=\"board\"><ol class=\"sequence\" aria-label=\"Your action sequence\"><li><b>1</b>Choose the next action below</li><li><b>2</b>Choose the next action below</li><li><b>3</b>Choose the next action below</li><li><b>4</b>Choose the next action below</li></ol><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\">Review sign-in and recovery settings and secure the account</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\">Preserve the supplied alert and event details; verify with Asha through a known channel</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\">Escalate the possible data exposure to the responsible teacher</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\">With the account owner, revoke the unrecognised session through the known service</button></div><div class=\"controls\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"secondary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-rotate-ccw\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8\"></path><path d=\"M3 3v5h5\"></path></svg>Undo last action</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Run sequence</button></div></div></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this record to explain your decisions to your teacher. Your explanation is reviewed separately from the automatic checks.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "SequenceBoard",
                  "steps": [
                    "Preserve the supplied alert and event details; verify with Asha through a known channel",
                    "With the account owner, revoke the unrecognised session through the known service",
                    "Review sign-in and recovery settings and secure the account",
                    "Escalate the possible data exposure to the responsible teacher"
                  ],
                  "success": "Response decision: preserve and verify the alert, revoke the unknown session with the owner, review account protection, and escalate the possible exposure to the responsible teacher. Urgent containment and escalation can overlap in a real incident."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "Kabir reconstructs an account alert",
            "icon": {},
            "panels": [
              {
                "heading": "A sign-in notification arrives",
                "facts": [
                  "09:00 Â· recognised school laptop",
                  "09:12 Â· unfamiliar session",
                  "A different city label appears"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "The unfamiliar session downloads a file",
                "facts": [
                  "09:14 Â· registrations.csv downloaded",
                  "09:20 Â· Asha does not recognise the session",
                  "The team needs to act without accusing someone"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Keep three kinds of statement separate",
                "facts": [
                  "Observation: what the supplied record says",
                  "Hypothesis: a possible explanation to verify",
                  "Unsupported claim: a conclusion the evidence cannot establish"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "What does the city label prove?",
                "facts": [
                  "Location labels may be approximate",
                  "An unfamiliar session merits checking",
                  "No supplied record identifies a particular student"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Preserve, verify and contain",
                "facts": [
                  "Keep the relevant alert and event details",
                  "Verify through a known channel with Asha",
                  "Review and revoke unrecognised sessions",
                  "Escalate possible data exposure to the teacher"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "A timeline is stronger than a guess",
                "facts": [
                  "Separate observed facts from explanations",
                  "Record missing evidence and uncertainty",
                  "Next: reconstruct, classify and respond to a fresh case"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "task": "A city label differs. Which conclusion is supported?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "It proves a particular student stole the file",
                "why": "The records do not identify an attacker. Do not turn a location label into an accusation."
              },
              {
                "label": "It is an indicator to verify with other evidence",
                "correct": true,
                "why": "Treat it as an indicator, then check the session and account owner's response."
              },
              {
                "label": "Delete the logs before anyone sees them",
                "why": "Deleting relevant records would destroy evidence needed for a responsible response."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lesson": {
            "id": "cyber-class-11-security-design-review",
            "slug": "security-design-review",
