          "practice": [
            {
              "stage": 0,
              "brief": "A security design must address its stated risks within real constraints. Test the controls, explain remaining risk and revise when new evidence appears.",
              "eyebrow": "Festival team security lab",
              "prompt": "Defend a festival security design within a 6-token budget.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">Budget: 6 tokens. Priorities: public registration exposure, gate laptop failure and password theft. Each control costs 2. Choose safeguards, then test the design.</p><label class=\"checkRow\"><input type=\"checkbox\"/><span><strong>Named access and prompt removal of former members</strong><small>2 tokens</small></span></label><label class=\"checkRow\"><input type=\"checkbox\"/><span><strong>Separate backup with a restoration test</strong><small>2 tokens</small></span></label><label class=\"checkRow\"><input type=\"checkbox\"/><span><strong>Individual accounts, MFA and private recovery</strong><small>2 tokens</small></span></label><label class=\"checkRow\"><input type=\"checkbox\"/><span><strong>Redesign the festival poster</strong><small>2 tokens</small></span></label><p class=\"cost\">Selected: 0 / 6 tokens</p><button class=\"secondary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Run design test</button><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Save design</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this record to explain your decisions to your teacher. Your explanation is reviewed separately from the automatic checks.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 1,
              "brief": "A security design must address its stated risks within real constraints. Test the controls, explain remaining risk and revise when new evidence appears.",
              "eyebrow": "Festival team security lab",
              "prompt": "Explain a remaining risk and a proportionate response.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"></path></svg><strong>Residual risk hearing</strong></div><p class=\"callout\">The team has all three safeguards. Explain which risk still remains and what the team should do about it.</p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">MFA guarantees nobody can ever expose data</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">An authorised organiser could still share data; use clear handling rules and an escalation route</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A backup makes access controls unnecessary</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Defend decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this record to explain your decisions to your teacher. Your explanation is reviewed separately from the automatic checks.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "A security design must address its stated risks within real constraints. Test the controls, explain remaining risk and revise when new evidence appears.",
              "eyebrow": "Festival team security lab",
              "prompt": "Revise the plan after a gate laptop is lost.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"></path></svg><strong>New evidence: laptop lost</strong></div><p class=\"callout\">The gate laptop is lost while an organiser&#x27;s session is still active. Your separate backup exists. The initial design needs an incident-response revision.</p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Keep using the lost laptop&#x27;s active session because MFA was enabled</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Revoke the lost device&#x27;s sessions, restrict exposure, verify the backup and inform the responsible teacher</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Delete every event log so private details cannot spread</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Defend decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this record to explain your decisions to your teacher. Your explanation is reviewed separately from the automatic checks.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "The festival team's security hearing",
            "icon": {},
            "panels": [
              {
                "heading": "The team presents its plan",
                "facts": [
                  "Risk: exposed registration folder",
                  "Risk: gate laptop failure",
                  "Risk: stolen password",
                  "Budget: 6 tokens"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Every choice has a cost",
                "facts": [
                  "Named access: 2 tokens",
                  "Tested separate backup: 2 tokens",
                  "Protected individual accounts: 2 tokens",
                  "Poster redesign: 2 tokens"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Match controls to failure modes",
                "facts": [
                  "Named access â†’ reduces public exposure",
                  "Tested backup â†’ supports recovery",
                  "MFA and recovery â†’ protect sign-in",
                  "No control removes every risk"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Does the backup protect confidentiality?",
                "facts": [
                  "A backup can recover lost information",
                  "It does not remove a public sharing link",
                  "The exposed folder needs an access-control change"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "New evidence arrives",
                "facts": [
                  "A laptop is lost with an active session",
                  "MFA does not automatically end that session",
                  "Revoke access, assess exposure and verify the backup with the teacher"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Defend the design, including its limits",
                "facts": [
                  "Explain each control and its cost",
                  "Name one remaining risk",
                  "Revise the design when evidence changes",
                  "Next: complete the module's design review"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "task": "Which control directly reduces a public registration-folder exposure?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "A tested backup alone",
                "why": "A backup supports recovery but does not restrict the public link."
              },
              {
                "label": "A more colourful poster",
                "why": "Poster design does not control who can open registrations."
              },
              {
                "label": "Named access and review of sharing links",
                "correct": true,
                "why": "This directly changes who can reach the exposed data."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "catalogue": [
        {
          "file": "app/module/cyber/lessons/senior/SecurityStories.tsx",
          "entries": [
            {
              "line": 15,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Asha's festival risk desk"
            },
            {
              "line": 17,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "One festival. Three things to protect."
            },
            {
              "line": 17,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Registration list Â· private contact details"
            },
            {
              "line": 17,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Payment sheet Â· accurate supplier amounts"
            },
            {
              "line": 17,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Gate laptop Â· available when visitors arrive"
            },
            {
              "line": 18,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The link escaped the team"
            },
            {
              "line": 18,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Registrations.csv: anyone with the link can view"
            },
            {
              "line": 18,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A supplier forwards the link to a public group"
            },
            {
              "line": 18,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Student contact details could be copied"
            },
            {
              "line": 19,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Describe the chain"
            },
            {
              "line": 19,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Asset: the registration list"
            },
            {
              "line": 19,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Threat: an unauthorised person downloads it"
            },
            {
              "line": 19,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Vulnerability: public-link sharing"
            },
            {
              "line": 19,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Control: named access for organisers"
            },
            {
              "line": 20,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "What is the weakness?"
            },
            {
              "line": 20,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The registration list contains information worth protecting."
            },
            {
              "line": 20,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A harmful download is a possible event."
            },
            {
              "line": 20,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Find the setting that makes that event easier."
            },
            {
              "line": 21,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Now the team can act"
            },
            {
              "line": 21,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Restrict the link to named organisers"
            },
            {
              "line": 21,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Check what was exposed with the teacher"
            },
            {
              "line": 21,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Record what is known and what remains uncertain"
            },
            {
              "line": 22,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Protect more than secrecy"
            },
            {
              "line": 22,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Confidentiality: who can see contacts?"
            },
            {
              "line": 22,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Integrity: who can change amounts?"
            },
            {
              "line": 22,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Availability: will the gate system work?"
            },
            {
              "line": 22,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Next: build and prioritise your risk register"
            },
            {
              "line": 23,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose the vulnerability in the registration-list case."
            },
            {
              "line": 24,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The registration list"
            },
            {
              "line": 24,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The list is the asset. Which setting makes unwanted access possible?"
            },
            {
              "line": 25,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Anyone-with-link sharing"
            },
            {
              "line": 25,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The open sharing setting is the vulnerability."
            },
            {
              "line": 26,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "An unauthorised download"
            },
            {
              "line": 26,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "That is a threat event. Identify the weakness it could use."
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Kabir's missing sign-in phone"
            },
            {
              "line": 32,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The festival account needs its organiser"
            },
            {
              "line": 32,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Kabir uses an individual account"
            },
            {
              "line": 32,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A password manager stores a unique password"
            },
            {
              "line": 32,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "His phone provides the second sign-in factor"
            },
            {
              "line": 33,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The phone is missing"
            },
            {
              "line": 33,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Kabir still knows the official service address"
            },
            {
              "line": 33,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A recovery code exists"
            },
            {
              "line": 33,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "But where was that code stored?"
            },
            {
              "line": 34,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Plan for losing the sign-in device"
            },
            {
              "line": 34,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Password: long and unique"
            },
            {
              "line": 34,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "MFA or a supported passkey: stronger sign-in"
            },
            {
              "line": 34,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery: private and available independently of the lost phone"
            },
            {
              "line": 35,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose a usable recovery route"
            },
            {
              "line": 35,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The old phone is unavailable"
            },
            {
              "line": 35,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The team group includes suppliers"
            },
            {
              "line": 35,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "An offline recovery code is stored privately"
            },
            {
              "line": 36,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recover, then review"
            },
            {
              "line": 36,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Use the known provider's recovery process"
            },
            {
              "line": 36,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Review and revoke the lost device's sessions"
            },
            {
              "line": 36,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Register the replacement method and refresh recovery options"
            },
            {
              "line": 37,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Identity is only the first question"
            },
            {
              "line": 37,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Authentication: is this Kabir?"
            },
            {
              "line": 37,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Authorisation: what may Kabir access?"
            },
            {
              "line": 37,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Next: test protection, recovery and access decisions"
            },
            {
              "line": 38,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Where should a recovery code be available if the sign-in phone is lost?"
            },
            {
              "line": 39,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Only in a screenshot on that phone"
            },
            {
              "line": 39,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "That copy is unavailable with the phone. Recovery must survive the loss."
            },
            {
              "line": 40,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "In the festival's public group"
            },
            {
              "line": 40,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A recovery code can grant account access. Keep it private."
            },
            {
              "line": 41,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "In private storage independent of that phone"
            },
            {
              "line": 41,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery stays private and survives the lost device."
            },
            {
              "line": 45,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Asha's open festival folder"
            },
            {
              "line": 47,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fest Team Drive"
            },
            {
              "line": 47,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Asha updates registrations"
            },
            {
              "line": 47,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The teacher reads progress"
            },
            {
              "line": 47,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The supplier delivers equipment"
            },
            {
              "line": 48,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Everyone was made an editor"
            },
            {
              "line": 48,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Supplier: can read contact details"
            },
            {
              "line": 48,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Guest: can change the registration file"
            },
            {
              "line": 48,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Former organiser Dev: still in the organiser group"
            },
            {
              "line": 49,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Grant access for the task"
            },
            {
              "line": 49,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Registration lead: edit"
            },
            {
              "line": 49,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Oversight teacher: view"
            },
            {
              "line": 49,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Equipment supplier: no registration access"
            },
            {
              "line": 49,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Guest programme link: expire after the event"
            },
            {
              "line": 50,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "One share removed. Is access gone?"
            },
            {
              "line": 50,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Dev's direct share: removed"
            },
            {
              "line": 50,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Dev's organiser-group membership: active"
            },
            {
              "line": 50,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The organiser group can still open the folder"
            },
            {
              "line": 51,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Test every access route"
            },
            {
              "line": 51,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Remove former members from relevant groups"
            },
            {
              "line": 51,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Review direct shares and public links"
            },
            {
              "line": 51,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Test as the affected role before calling the change complete"
            },
            {
              "line": 52,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A smaller permission set still works"
            },
            {
              "line": 52,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Organisers can do their work"
            },
            {
              "line": 52,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Suppliers receive only delivery information"
            },
            {
              "line": 52,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Next: configure and test three access cases"
            },
            {
              "line": 53,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Dev has left. The direct share is removed but the organiser group still grants access. What should change?"
            },
            {
              "line": 54,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Nothing: the direct share was removed"
            },
            {
              "line": 54,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Group membership can still grant access. Check inherited permissions."
            },
            {
              "line": 55,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Remove Dev from the relevant group and test again"
            },
            {
              "line": 55,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Both direct and inherited access routes need review."
            },
            {
              "line": 56,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Make the whole folder public"
            },
            {
              "line": 56,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Public sharing would expose it to more people."
            },
            {
              "line": 60,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Kabir inspects the address bar"
            },
            {
              "line": 62,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A programme link arrives"
            },
            {
              "line": 62,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Display title: Cyberpur School Festival"
            },
