              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 139,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Restore a fictional duplicate"
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "At 10:30 the working file became empty. The expected count before corruption was 42 registrations. Choose a separate recoverable copy; keep the original evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 142,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 142,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Restore to a new practice folder"
            },
            {
              "line": 143,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "clean"
            },
            {
              "line": 143,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Restored copy: 42 readable records. Original remains untouched."
            },
            {
              "line": 143,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "same"
            },
            {
              "line": 143,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Restore failed: the copy was on the unavailable laptop."
            },
            {
              "line": 143,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Restored copy: 0 records. The corruption was synced."
            },
            {
              "line": 144,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery record: restored the separate 10:00 version to a new folder, confirmed 42 readable records and preserved the original."
            },
            {
              "line": 144,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 144,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Verify restoration"
            },
            {
              "line": 146,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Compare all 43 expected IDs and statuses"
            },
            {
              "line": 146,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Test that the gate account can read the restored copy"
            },
            {
              "line": 146,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Declare success because the file icon exists"
            },
            {
              "line": 146,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep the original and record the restoration result"
            },
            {
              "line": 149,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "New case: the gate export should have 43 registrations. The restored file opens, and its last rows are shown below. Decide what to check before declaring recovery."
            },
            {
              "line": 150,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 152,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Unseen recovery plan: verify all 43 IDs and statuses, test the gate account's access, preserve the original and record the result. A file opening alone is insufficient."
            },
            {
              "line": 152,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Check completeness and actual user access, and preserve the original. A file icon alone does not prove a successful recovery."
            },
            {
              "line": 152,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 152,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Approve recovery checks"
            },
            {
              "line": 157,
              "kind": "Dynamic template",
              "text": "${event.time} Â· ${event.text}"
            },
            {
              "line": 157,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Timeline: recognised sign-in 09:00 â†’ unfamiliar session 09:12 â†’ download 09:14 â†’ owner does not recognise it 09:20. This supports escalation, not an accusation."
            },
            {
              "line": 158,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Hypothesis to verify"
            },
            {
              "line": 158,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Unsupported conclusion"
            },
            {
              "line": 158,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Observed in supplied records"
            },
            {
              "line": 158,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Evidence ledger: download is observed, unauthorised access is a hypothesis, and a city label does not identify an attacker."
            },
            {
              "line": 159,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "New case: a login alert and an unknown download arrive while the account owner is in class. The teacher is available. Follow the exerciseâ€™s initial-response sequence without contacting suspected users or deleting records."
            },
            {
              "line": 159,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Response decision: preserve and verify the alert, revoke the unknown session with the owner, review account protection, and escalate the possible exposure to the responsible teacher. Urgent containment and escalation can overlap in a real incident."
            },
            {
              "line": 168,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Budget: 6 tokens. Priorities: public registration exposure, gate laptop failure and password theft. Each control costs 2. Choose safeguards, then test the design."
            },
            {
              "line": 169,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "tokens"
            },
            {
              "line": 170,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Selected:"
            },
            {
              "line": 170,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "/ 6 tokens"
            },
            {
              "line": 171,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 171,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Run design test"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": ":"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "safeguard present"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "unaddressed"
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The design exceeds the 6-token budget. Keep controls that address the stated risks."
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A stated risk remains unaddressed. A poster redesign cannot replace access control, account protection or a recoverable backup."
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Design: named access (2), tested separate backup (2), protected individual accounts (2). All three priorities have a control within the 6-token budget."
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Save design"
            },
            {
              "line": 177,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "MFA guarantees nobody can ever expose data"
            },
            {
              "line": 178,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "An authorised organiser could still share data; use clear handling rules and an escalation route"
            },
            {
              "line": 179,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A backup makes access controls unnecessary"
            },
            {
              "line": 181,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep using the lost laptop's active session because MFA was enabled"
            },
            {
              "line": 182,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Revoke the lost device's sessions, restrict exposure, verify the backup and inform the responsible teacher"
            },
            {
              "line": 183,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Delete every event log so private details cannot spread"
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Residual risk hearing"
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "New evidence: laptop lost"
            },
            {
              "line": 186,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The team has all three safeguards. Explain which risk still remains and what the team should do about it."
            },
            {
              "line": 186,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The gate laptop is lost while an organiser's session is still active. Your separate backup exists. The initial design needs an incident-response revision."
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Residual risk: authorised people can still misuse or accidentally share data. Handling rules, oversight and an escalation route reduce this risk without claiming to eliminate it."
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Design revision: revoke lost-device sessions, assess data exposure with the teacher and test the separate backup. MFA does not automatically end an existing session."
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Controls reduce specific risks; none removes every risk. Consider what an already authorised organiser could still do."
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "MFA does not necessarily close an existing session. Preserve relevant records, revoke access with the owner and use the tested backup."
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 188,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Defend decision"
            },
            {
              "line": 193,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "An asset has value. A threat could harm it. A vulnerability is a weakness. A control reduces risk. Explain confidentiality, integrity and availability separately."
            },
            {
              "line": 193,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Build the festival team's first risk chain."
            },
            {
              "line": 193,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Match each incident to its main security impact."
            },
            {
              "line": 193,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Prioritise three risks and justify each one with evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 194,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Protect sign-in and recovery together. Authentication checks identity; authorisation limits what that identity can do. Never enter real passwords or recovery codes here."
            },
            {
              "line": 194,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Protect Asha's fictional festival account."
            },
            {
              "line": 194,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The sign-in phone is lost. Rehearse recovery without the phone."
            },
            {
              "line": 194,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A new supplier can sign in. Does that mean they may edit every file?"
            },
            {
              "line": 195,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Least privilege means granting only the access a task needs, for only as long as it is needed. Test direct shares, groups and public links."
            },
            {
              "line": 196,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Read the full hostname and check the task. HTTPS protects a connection but does not prove that a site is legitimate. Every address in this exercise is fictional."
            },
            {
              "line": 197,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Follow the purpose from collection through storage, access and deletion. Collect less and restrict access. Apply the supplied exercise policy; retention periods depend on context."
            },
            {
              "line": 198,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Trusted updates, locks and recoverable backups address different risks. A synced copy may repeat damage. Restore a duplicate and verify its contents and access."
            },
            {
              "line": 198,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Repair the shared laptop's protection plan."
            },
            {
              "line": 198,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The registration file was corrupted. Recover a usable copy."
            },
            {
              "line": 198,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A different gate export should have 43 records. What proves recovery?"
            },
            {
              "line": 199,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Separate recorded observations from hypotheses and accusations. Preserve relevant evidence, verify independently and involve the account owner and responsible teacher."
            },
            {
              "line": 199,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Reconstruct the supplied account timeline."
            },
            {
              "line": 199,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Label each claim by what the evidence supports."
            },
            {
              "line": 199,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Handle a fresh unknown-session case using the stated initial-response sequence."
            },
            {
              "line": 200,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A security design must address its stated risks within real constraints. Test the controls, explain remaining risk and revise when new evidence appears."
            },
            {
              "line": 200,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Defend a festival security design within a 6-token budget."
            },
            {
              "line": 200,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Explain a remaining risk and a proportionate response."
            },
            {
              "line": 200,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Revise the plan after a gate laptop is lost."
            },
            {
              "line": 208,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "your-digital-risk-map"
            },
            {
              "line": 208,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "identity-beyond-a-password"
            },
            {
              "line": 209,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "devices-updates-and-backups"
            },
            {
              "line": 210,
              "kind": "Dynamic template",
              "text": "evidence-${props.lesson.slug}"
            },
            {
              "line": 212,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "object"
            },
            {
              "line": 217,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Festival team security lab"
            },
            {
              "line": 217,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "lab"
            },
            {
              "line": 218,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Your evidence record"
            },
            {
              "line": 218,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Use this record to explain your decisions to your teacher. Your explanation is reviewed separately from the automatic checks."
            }
