              "title": "Examples and a rule",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Asha compares a handwritten rule with a tiny learned predictor. In this lab, each fictional sample has two numerical features and a material label. A nearest-example method predicts from the closest labelled training examples.",
              "dialogue": "The examples can change the predictions.",
              "status": "Planning the experiment",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 14.72,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ai-sorting-lab.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Examples and a rule</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ai-sorting-lab.webp\" alt=\"Asha and Kabir compare paper, metal and plastic practice samples with a laptop classifier at a school festival workbench.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>The team changes examples, checks predictions and keeps a person responsible for the result.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "how-a-model-learns-2",
              "label": "The problem",
              "title": "Only one kind of example",
              "mood": "surprise",
              "caption": "The first training selection contains paper examples only. A new metal-like sample is still compared with paper because the model has never been shown the other label. A model cannot gain missing coverage from a confident-looking display.",
              "dialogue": "What did we actually show it?",
              "status": "Checking the problem",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 15.37,
              "duration": 14.549,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Only one kind of example</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Tiny nearest-example classifier</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Training at first</span><strong>P1, P2: Paper only</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Missing coverage</span><strong>No Metal examples selected</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Held-out labels</span><strong>Kept out of training</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Equal-nearest disagreement</span><strong>Request human review</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "how-a-model-learns-3",
              "label": "How it works",
              "title": "Keep the test separate",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "Training examples shape the model. Held-out examples check it after the choices are made. Classification predicts categories, regression predicts numerical values and clustering groups similar examples without provided group labels. This lab uses a deliberately tiny classification method.",
              "dialogue": "Testing is not another chance to teach from the answers.",
              "status": "Understanding the method",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 30.569,
              "duration": 18.347,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Keep the test separate</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Classification predicts categories</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Training labels shape the predictor</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Held-out labels remain outside training</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "how-a-model-learns-4",
              "label": "Your decision",
              "title": "Protect the evaluation",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "A teammate wants to reveal test labels and copy them into training before reporting the score. Choose the action that preserves a meaningful independent check. The test examples must stay outside the training selection.",
              "dialogue": "Do we still have an unseen test?",
              "status": "Your turn",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 49.566,
              "duration": 13.717,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Protect the evaluation</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Tiny nearest-example classifier</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Training at first</span><strong>P1, P2: Paper only</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Missing coverage</span><strong>No Metal examples selected</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Held-out labels</span><strong>Kept out of training</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Equal-nearest disagreement</span><strong>Request human review</strong></div></div><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"storyQuestion\"><strong>Should the team copy revealed test labels into training before reporting that same test score?</strong></p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Yes: any higher score is progress</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">No: preserve an independent held-out check</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Yes: the interface still calls it a test</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\">Test my decision</button></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "how-a-model-learns-5",
              "label": "What changes",
              "title": "Observe the learner",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "The team adds the missing training label and runs the held-out examples before revealing their labels. If equally close examples disagree, this toy model asks for human review. Its result is an educational demonstration, not a reliable material detector.",
              "dialogue": "A small demonstration can show a method without proving reliability.",
              "status": "Reviewing the evidence",
              "tone": "resolved",
              "start": 63.933,
              "duration": 17.088,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Observe the learner</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-flask-conical\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2\"></path><path d=\"M6.453 15h11.094\"></path><path d=\"M8.5 2h7\"></path></svg><strong>Tiny nearest-example classifier</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Training at first</span><strong>P1, P2: Paper only</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Missing coverage</span><strong>M1, M2 Metal examples added</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Held-out labels</span><strong>Revealed after predictions committed</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Equal-nearest disagreement</span><strong>Request human review</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
