              "caption": "Kabir asks a fictional assistant to draft festival instructions from a fixed source pack. The pack includes a volunteer memo and a practice safety note. A fluent answer arrives with some correct statements and some unsupported ones.",
              "dialogue": "Which source actually supports each sentence?",
              "status": "Planning the experiment",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 14.955,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ai-source-desk.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-search\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"8\"></circle><path d=\"m21 21-4.3-4.3\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 AI experiment</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">The research desk</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ai-source-desk.webp\" alt=\"Asha and Kabir compare a laptop assistant response with a printed memo, open reference book and source folder in the school library.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>The actual source passage determines which assistant claims the team can support.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Fictional examples and prepared outputs. No private records or external AI account required.</small></div>"
            },
            {
