            {
              "line": 98,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Repair the labels without inventing missing observations."
            },
            {
              "line": 98,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Decide what to do with duplicate and conflicting records."
            },
            {
              "line": 98,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Write a defensible data-card decision for a bright-only collection."
            },
            {
              "line": 99,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Training examples shape predictions; held-out examples evaluate them. This tiny nearest-example classifier uses invented numerical features and is not a real material detector."
