          "scenes": [
            {
              "id": "reuse-a-reliable-step-1",
              "label": "Meet the team",
              "title": "One check in three places",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Kabir notices that the enquiry screen, review list and response preview each contain a copied version of the exercise rule. One copy has already drifted to a different threshold. Repeating the code has repeated the opportunity for inconsistency.",
              "dialogue": "Can one reliable step serve every caller?",
              "status": "Planning the workflow",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 15.915,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ct-scholarship-desk.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-git-branch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"6\" x2=\"6\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"15\"></line><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"></circle><path d=\"M18 9a9 9 0 0 1-9 9\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 workflow desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">One check in three places</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-11/ct-scholarship-desk.webp\" alt=\"Asha sorts anonymous enquiry cards into trays while Kabir checks a laptop record table, with a teacher available in the school library.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>The team separates intake, rule checking, teacher review and communication before automating the workflow.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Fictional records and criteria. The simulation makes no real awards or payments.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "reuse-a-reliable-step-2",
              "label": "The problem",
              "title": "The copies disagree",
              "mood": "surprise",
              "caption": "The same record is marked differently depending on which screen checks it. The team needs one shared function with a clear contract rather than three almost-identical sets of conditions. Moving the code must preserve input validation and review paths.",
              "dialogue": "Reuse the check without losing its safeguards.",
              "status": "Investigating a problem",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 16.565,
              "duration": 15.787,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-git-branch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"6\" x2=\"6\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"15\"></line><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"></circle><path d=\"M18 9a9 9 0 0 1-9 9\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 workflow desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">The copies disagree</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg><strong>One shared validated function</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>B20 Â· 60 / complete</span><strong>Eligible</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>C30 Â· 59 / complete</span><strong>Not eligible</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>D40 Â· 65 / incomplete</span><strong>Needs documents</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Score absent</span><strong>Review missing data</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records and criteria. The simulation makes no real awards or payments.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "reuse-a-reliable-step-3",
              "label": "How it works",
              "title": "Describe the contract",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "State the functionâ€™s input, output and expectations. Use stable IDs, validated scores and explicit document status. A missing field is not automatically zero or false. A shared function must return a visible review result when required information is absent.",
              "dialogue": "An absent value is a real case to handle.",
              "status": "Tracing the reasoning",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 33.001,
              "duration": 18.069,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-git-branch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"6\" x2=\"6\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"15\"></line><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"></circle><path d=\"M18 9a9 9 0 0 1-9 9\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 workflow desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Describe the contract</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Define input, output and validation</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Share the check instead of copying inconsistent rules</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Missing, zero and false are different states</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records and criteria. The simulation makes no real awards or payments.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "reuse-a-reliable-step-4",
              "label": "Your decision",
              "title": "Handle a missing score",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "A record has no score value but its documents are complete. Should the shared check silently convert the missing score to zero, mark the record eligible, or return the defined missing-data review route?",
              "dialogue": "Missing is not a numeric score.",
              "status": "Your turn",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 51.721,
              "duration": 12.693,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-git-branch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"6\" x2=\"6\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"15\"></line><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"></circle><path d=\"M18 9a9 9 0 0 1-9 9\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 workflow desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Handle a missing score</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg><strong>One shared validated function</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>B20 Â· 60 / complete</span><strong>Eligible</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>C30 Â· 59 / complete</span><strong>Not eligible</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>D40 Â· 65 / incomplete</span><strong>Needs documents</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Score absent</span><strong>Review missing data</strong></div></div><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"storyQuestion\"><strong>The score field is absent but documents are complete. What should the shared check return?</strong></p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Review missing data</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Treat the missing score as zero</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Eligible because documents are complete</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\">Test my decision</button></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records and criteria. The simulation makes no real awards or payments.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "reuse-a-reliable-step-5",
              "label": "What changes",
              "title": "Use the same function",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "The team runs the same validated function for several records and sees consistent outcomes. Complete and incomplete document flags remain distinct from an unknown flag. The review list and response preview can now share one rule without losing validation.",
              "dialogue": "One correction can reach all the callers.",
              "status": "Checking the correction",
              "tone": "resolved",
              "start": 65.064,
              "duration": 17.131,
