              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-list-checks\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m3 17 2 2 4-4\"></path><path d=\"m3 7 2 2 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M13 6h8\"></path><path d=\"M13 12h8\"></path><path d=\"M13 18h8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 11 workflow desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Enter the logic lab</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Revised exercise threshold: score â‰¥ 70</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Retest validation, missing and duplicate protections</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Preserve evidence and keep human authority</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records and criteria. The simulation makes no real awards or payments.</small></div>"
            }
          ],
          "practice": [
            {
              "stage": 0,
              "brief": "Defend correctness, limitations and alternatives. A new at-least-70 requirement changes some expected outcomes while input, duplicate and human-review protections still matter.",
              "eyebrow": "Scholarship workflow logic lab",
              "prompt": "Update the shared threshold and run the revised six-case pack.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">Revised fictional requirement: score â‰¥ 70 AND complete documents. The expected outcomes below follow that new brief; empty, missing and duplicate safeguards still apply.</p><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Shared score threshold</span><select><option selected=\"\">60</option><option>70</option></select></label><button class=\"secondary\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Run revised test pack</button><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Save test record</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your algorithm evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the trace, expected outcomes and revisions to explain your reasoning. Your teacher reviews the individual defence separately.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 1,
              "brief": "Defend correctness, limitations and alternatives. A new at-least-70 requirement changes some expected outcomes while input, duplicate and human-review protections still matter.",
              "eyebrow": "Scholarship workflow logic lab",
              "prompt": "Compare two designs on consistency, validation and maintainability.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Copy the threshold into every screen and skip validation to save time</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Use one shared validated check, retest affected and unchanged behaviour, and keep teacher review</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Choose the algorithm with the prettiest output even when its trace is wrong</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your algorithm evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the trace, expected outcomes and revisions to explain your reasoning. Your teacher reviews the individual defence separately.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Copy the threshold into every screen and skip validation to save time",
                    "Use one shared validated check, retest affected and unchanged behaviour, and keep teacher review",
                    "Choose the algorithm with the prettiest output even when its trace is wrong"
                  ],
                  "answer": 1,
                  "feedback": "Compare correctness, validation and maintainability. A shared check reduces drift, but still needs tests and an explicit human decision point.",
                  "success": "Design defence: one shared validated check avoids conflicting copies; retest affected outcomes and unchanged protections. A different design needs evidence for correctness and its extra maintenance effort. Real decisions stay with the teacher."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Defend correctness, limitations and alternatives. A new at-least-70 requirement changes some expected outcomes while input, duplicate and human-review protections still matter.",
              "eyebrow": "Scholarship workflow logic lab",
              "prompt": "Defend a response to a fresh pair of conflicting records.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"tableWrap\"><table class=\"table\"><caption>Unseen case Â· conflicting records</caption><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Score</th><th>Documents</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>B20</th><td>72</td><td>Complete</td></tr><tr><th>B20</th><td>45</td><td>Complete</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Pick 72 because it gives the desired outcome and delete the other record</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Award a real scholarship from the higher score</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Preserve both records, flag the duplicate, seek authorised review and add this conflict to the tests</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div><p class=\"micro\">Explain the decision and one alternative to your teacher. Structured checks do not automatically assess an individual oral defence.</p></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your algorithm evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the trace, expected outcomes and revisions to explain your reasoning. Your teacher reviews the individual defence separately.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Pick 72 because it gives the desired outcome and delete the other record",
                    "Award a real scholarship from the higher score",
                    "Preserve both records, flag the duplicate, seek authorised review and add this conflict to the tests"
                  ],
                  "answer": 2,
                  "feedback": "The duplicate identity conflict is unresolved. A high score cannot justify overwriting evidence, choosing a convenient row or making a real award.",
                  "success": "Unseen defence: preserve the conflicting B20 records, flag the duplicate and refer it for authorised review. Add the conflict to regression evidence; a correct threshold alone cannot resolve identity ambiguity."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "The algorithm review board",
            "concepts": [
              "Revised exercise threshold: score â‰¥ 70",
              "Retest validation, missing and duplicate protections",
              "Preserve evidence and keep human authority"
            ],
            "question": "Under the revised rule, a valid record scores exactly 70 with complete documents. What should it return?",
            "choices": [
              "Not eligible because the old threshold was 60",
              "A real award without review",
              "Eligible under the revised exercise rule"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "why": "The new inclusive boundary includes 70. This changes an exercise check, not responsibility for real award decisions."
          }
        }
