            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Six-case matrix: ordinary 72 â†’ Eligible; exact 60 â†’ Eligible; 59 â†’ Not eligible; empty list handled; duplicate IDs flagged; missing score â†’ Review missing data. Expected outcomes were stated before execution."
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Passing these examples does not prove correctness for every possible input"
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State the limit of the evidence too: a finite set of passing examples is not proof for every possible input."
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fresh-case record: 75/incomplete â†’ Needs documents; âˆ’1 â†’ Invalid record; supplied 0 â†’ Not eligible rather than missing. Passing these cases still does not prove every possible input."
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Copy the threshold into every screen and skip validation to save time"
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Use one shared validated check, retest affected and unchanged behaviour, and keep teacher review"
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose the algorithm with the prettiest output even when its trace is wrong"
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Compare correctness, validation and maintainability. A shared check reduces drift, but still needs tests and an explicit human decision point."
            },
            {
              "line": 140,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Design defence: one shared validated check avoids conflicting copies; retest affected outcomes and unchanged protections. A different design needs evidence for correctness and its extra maintenance effort. Real decisions stay with the teacher."
            },
            {
              "line": 141,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Unseen case Â· conflicting records"
