            {
              "id": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk-1",
              "label": "Meet the team",
              "title": "A service with many users",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Asha and Kabir move from protecting one account to designing a fictional college-festival portal. Students register, organisers manage entries and a supplier sees only the programme. A failure can now affect people who never made the unsafe decision.",
              "dialogue": "Who owns the risk for the whole service?",
              "status": "Inspect the system",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 16.363,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/portal-design-room.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">A service with many users</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/portal-design-room.webp\" alt=\"Asha and Kabir arrange client, server and database concept tiles at a school makerspace table while a teacher helps discuss a trust boundary.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>Different actors cross different trust boundaries. Place each safeguard where its rule is enforced.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk-2",
              "label": "The problem",
              "title": "Map assets and actors",
              "mood": "surprise",
              "caption": "The registration database, identities and gate availability are assets. Students, organisers, suppliers and the service provider have different roles. Requests cross trust boundaries from a browser into a server and then into stored data.",
              "dialogue": "A signed-in user is not automatically allowed every record.",
              "status": "Risk unresolved",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 17.013,
              "duration": 15.744,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Map assets and actors</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>System risk register Â· simulation</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Private contacts</span><strong>Public export Â· supplied risk score 9 Â· registration lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Gate availability</span><strong>Single device Â· score 6 Â· operations lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Programme poster</span><strong>Editable copy Â· score 2 Â· communications lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Remaining risk</span><strong>Each owner reviews controls and unresolved dependencies</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk-3",
              "label": "How it works",
              "title": "Risk needs an owner",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "Separate the harmful event, the weakness, the safeguard and the person responsible for checking it. Use the supplied likelihood and impact estimates to prioritise this exercise. A numerical score supports a discussion; it does not measure real risk precisely.",
              "dialogue": "Every priority needs evidence and an accountable owner.",
              "status": "Build the control",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 33.407,
              "duration": 16.875,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Risk needs an owner</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Assets + actors + trust boundaries</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Authentication is not per-record permission</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Prioritise with supplied estimates; name an owner and remaining risk</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk-4",
              "label": "Your decision",
              "title": "Choose the access boundary",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "A supplier signs in successfully but has no registration task. Should sign-in grant the supplier all records, should the team share one organiser password, or should the server restrict access to the supplierâ€™s authorised purpose?",
              "dialogue": "Authentication and authorisation remain different checks.",
              "status": "Decision required",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 50.931,
              "duration": 14.507,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Choose the access boundary</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>System risk register Â· simulation</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Private contacts</span><strong>Public export Â· supplied risk score 9 Â· registration lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Gate availability</span><strong>Single device Â· score 6 Â· operations lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Programme poster</span><strong>Editable copy Â· score 2 Â· communications lead</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Remaining risk</span><strong>Each owner reviews controls and unresolved dependencies</strong></div></div><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"storyQuestion\"><strong>A supplier signs in but has no registration task. What access should the server allow?</strong></p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">All records because sign-in succeeded</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A shared organiser password</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Only the supplierâ€™s authorised programme task</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\">Test my decision</button></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk-5",
              "label": "What changes",
              "title": "A shared responsibility map",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Asha assigns an owner for registration access, a gate fallback and supplier permissions. The team records what could still fail after controls are applied. No individual promise removes the serviceâ€™s need for tested safeguards.",
              "dialogue": "An owner checks the control and the remaining risk.",
              "status": "Evidence updated",
              "tone": "resolved",
