            {
              "stage": 0,
              "brief": "A browser, server, database and external provider have different jobs. DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport; neither grants record permission. This is a conceptual architecture, not a real deployment.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Assign each component its job.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption>Fictional college-fest portal Â· trust changes at each arrow</figcaption><ol><li><div><strong>Browser</strong><span>Untrusted client input; display responses</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Application server</strong><span>Trusted session + action permission + validation</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Database</strong><span>Constrained service access; private records</span></div></li></ol><p>DNS locates the hostname; HTTPS protects the connection. External payment status crosses a separate server/provider verification boundary.</p></figure><div class=\"board\"><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Browser / client</span><select aria-label=\"Browser / client\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles</option><option>Check session, action permission and input before data access</option><option>Store records behind constrained service access</option><option>Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Application server</span><select aria-label=\"Application server\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles</option><option>Check session, action permission and input before data access</option><option>Store records behind constrained service access</option><option>Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Database</span><select aria-label=\"Database\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles</option><option>Check session, action permission and input before data access</option><option>Store records behind constrained service access</option><option>Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>DNS and HTTPS</span><select aria-label=\"DNS and HTTPS\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles</option><option>Check session, action permission and input before data access</option><option>Store records behind constrained service access</option><option>Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access</option></select></label><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check my map</button></div></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "MatchTable",
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "label": "Browser / client",
                      "answer": "Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles",
                      "why": "A client can change requests; the server owns enforcement."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Application server",
                      "answer": "Check session, action permission and input before data access",
                      "why": "The service must enforce the decision beyond the browser."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Database",
                      "answer": "Store records behind constrained service access",
                      "why": "Public browsers should not carry database credentials."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "DNS and HTTPS",
                      "answer": "Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access",
                      "why": "Neither substitutes for application authorisation or verifies the operatorâ€™s legitimacy."
                    }
                  ],
                  "options": [
                    "Collect input and display responses; do not trust it to assign roles",
                    "Check session, action permission and input before data access",
                    "Store records behind constrained service access",
                    "Locate the hostname and protect transport, without granting record access"
                  ],
                  "success": "Architecture roles: browser gathers/displays untrusted input; server enforces identity, permission and validation; database stays behind constrained service access; DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport without granting application permission."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 1,
              "brief": "A browser, server, database and external provider have different jobs. DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport; neither grants record permission. This is a conceptual architecture, not a real deployment.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Place the three controls at the boundary that owns them.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption>Fictional college-fest portal Â· trust changes at each arrow</figcaption><ol><li><div><strong>Browser</strong><span>Untrusted client input; display responses</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Application server</strong><span>Trusted session + action permission + validation</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Database</strong><span>Constrained service access; private records</span></div></li></ol><p>DNS locates the hostname; HTTPS protects the connection. External payment status crosses a separate server/provider verification boundary.</p></figure><div class=\"board\"><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Trusted session identity and record permission</span><select aria-label=\"Trusted session identity and record permission\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Application server before private data access</option><option>Server-to-database boundary</option><option>Payment-provider integration boundary on the server</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Least-privilege database account and structured data access</span><select aria-label=\"Least-privilege database account and structured data access\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Application server before private data access</option><option>Server-to-database boundary</option><option>Payment-provider integration boundary on the server</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Authenticity, reference and expected amount of payment status</span><select aria-label=\"Authenticity, reference and expected amount of payment status\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Application server before private data access</option><option>Server-to-database boundary</option><option>Payment-provider integration boundary on the server</option></select></label><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check my map</button></div></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "MatchTable",
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "label": "Trusted session identity and record permission",
                      "answer": "Application server before private data access",
                      "why": "A hidden client button or a client-provided role can be bypassed."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Least-privilege database account and structured data access",
                      "answer": "Server-to-database boundary",
                      "why": "Constrain the service account and keep supplied values separate from query instructions."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Authenticity, reference and expected amount of payment status",
                      "answer": "Payment-provider integration boundary on the server",
                      "why": "A browser message saying paid is insufficient; use the providerâ€™s documented trusted verification path."
                    }
                  ],
                  "options": [
                    "Application server before private data access",
                    "Server-to-database boundary",
                    "Payment-provider integration boundary on the server"
                  ],
                  "success": "Control locations: trusted session and per-record permission before private data access on the server; constrained service account and structured access at the database boundary; authentic expected payment status at the server/provider boundary using the providerâ€™s documented verification route."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "A browser, server, database and external provider have different jobs. DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport; neither grants record permission. This is a conceptual architecture, not a real deployment.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Defend the architectureâ€™s assumptions and limits.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Assume HTTPS proves the operator is legitimate and every browser payment status is genuine</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">State that the diagram assumes a trusted server identity source and documented provider verification; HTTPS protects only the connection</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Store database and provider secrets in the browser to reduce friction</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Assume HTTPS proves the operator is legitimate and every browser payment status is genuine",
                    "State that the diagram assumes a trusted server identity source and documented provider verification; HTTPS protects only the connection",
                    "Store database and provider secrets in the browser to reduce friction"
                  ],
                  "answer": 1,
                  "feedback": "A transport-protected connection does not establish operator legitimacy, a trusted role or payment proof. Keep server identity and provider verification assumptions explicit; no secret belongs in public client code.",
                  "success": "Architecture defence: assumed trusted session source and documented provider verification must be implemented and tested. HTTPS protects the connection to the hostname; it does not certify the operator, authorise a record or prove a payment. This conceptual diagram is not assurance of a real service."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "Kabir places the portal controls",
            "concepts": [
              "Browser claims are untrusted input",
              "Enforce session and record permission on the server",
              "DNS and HTTPS do not grant database access"
            ],
            "question": "Where should permission to read a private registration be enforced?",
            "choices": [
              "On the server using trusted session and record data",
              "Only by hiding a browser button",
              "In a shared password sent to everyone"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "why": "The server owns enforcement; a client-controlled role or hidden button cannot be the final access check."
          }
