          "lockedHint": "Complete the system decision first.",
          "source": "app/module/cyber/lessons/new/story/chapters/security-assurance-review.json",
          "duration": 102.737,
          "scenes": [
            {
              "id": "security-assurance-review-1",
              "label": "Meet the team",
              "title": "The security assurance review",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Kabir prepares the portal design for an individual review. The portfolio contains a risk register, boundary controls, an evidence timeline, an incident action log and a recovery test. The reviewer asks how cost, privacy and usability shaped the design.",
              "dialogue": "Who owns the remaining risk?",
              "status": "Inspect the system",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 16.832,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/portal-design-room.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">The security assurance review</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/portal-design-room.webp\" alt=\"Asha and Kabir arrange client, server and database concept tiles at a school makerspace table while a teacher helps discuss a trust boundary.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>Different actors cross different trust boundaries. Place each safeguard where its rule is enforced.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "security-assurance-review-2",
              "label": "The problem",
              "title": "New evidence changes the story",
              "mood": "surprise",
              "caption": "An initial login alert is explained by authorised maintenance. Separately, the supplied access settings still confirm a public export link. One benign alert does not cancel independent evidence of exposure; the team must revise each conclusion separately.",
              "dialogue": "Do not let one correction erase unrelated evidence.",
              "status": "Risk unresolved",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 17.482,
              "duration": 17.152,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">New evidence changes the story</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Changed assurance scenario Â· simulation</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>New evidence</span><strong>Initial login alert was authorised maintenance</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Independent evidence</span><strong>Public export setting remains confirmed</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Decision</span><strong>Update only the conclusion supported by new evidence</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Owner / limit</span><strong>Service lead reviews scope; operations lead owns residual outage risk</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "security-assurance-review-3",
              "label": "How it works",
              "title": "Defend proportionate controls",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "Keep the registration data restricted, preserve evidence, allow suppliers to publish only the programme and maintain tested recovery. Assign an owner and review point for residual supplier failure. Explain the tradeoff rather than claiming all risks are gone.",
              "dialogue": "A useful defence connects action, evidence and limitation.",
              "status": "Build the control",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 35.284,
              "duration": 17.088,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Defend proportionate controls</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Balance privacy, usability and cost</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Revise only the conclusion the new evidence changes</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Name residual risk, owner and review point; teacher reviews the viva</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "security-assurance-review-4",
              "label": "Your decision",
              "title": "Choose the revised conclusion",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "The login alert is benign, but the public export setting is confirmed. Should the team dismiss everything, accuse the named user anyway, or correct the alert hypothesis while containing and reviewing the separate exposure?",
              "dialogue": "Update the conclusion supported by the new evidence.",
              "status": "Decision required",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 53.022,
              "duration": 14.165,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Choose the revised conclusion</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Changed assurance scenario Â· simulation</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>New evidence</span><strong>Initial login alert was authorised maintenance</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Independent evidence</span><strong>Public export setting remains confirmed</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Decision</span><strong>Update only the conclusion supported by new evidence</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Owner / limit</span><strong>Service lead reviews scope; operations lead owns residual outage risk</strong></div></div><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"storyQuestion\"><strong>Maintenance explains a login alert, but a public export is independently confirmed. What changes?</strong></p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Correct the login hypothesis while containing and reviewing the separate exposure</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Dismiss all evidence as false</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Accuse the account holder anyway</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\">Test my decision</button></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
