              "start": 86.237,
              "duration": 15.851,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 portal design room</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Enter the assurance lab</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Balance privacy, usability and cost</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Revise only the conclusion the new evidence changes</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Name residual risk, owner and review point; teacher reviews the viva</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models. No live scanning, exploitation, external messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            }
          ],
          "practice": [
            {
              "stage": 0,
              "brief": "Defend the portal architecture and playbook with risk ownership, cost, privacy and usability. New evidence explains the initial login alert as maintenance; the public export remains independently confirmed.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Connect each tradeoff to a control and risk owner.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Privacy versus supplier convenience</span><select aria-label=\"Privacy versus supplier convenience\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry</option><option>Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk</option><option>Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Availability versus limited budget</span><select aria-label=\"Availability versus limited budget\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry</option><option>Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk</option><option>Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Usability versus shared-account shortcuts</span><select aria-label=\"Usability versus shared-account shortcuts\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry</option><option>Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk</option><option>Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access</option></select></label><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check my map</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "MatchTable",
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "label": "Privacy versus supplier convenience",
                      "answer": "Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry",
                      "why": "Publishing a programme does not justify disclosing private contacts."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Availability versus limited budget",
                      "answer": "Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk",
                      "why": "A fallback supports continuity but cannot eliminate supplier failures."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Usability versus shared-account shortcuts",
                      "answer": "Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access",
                      "why": "A shared password hides accountability rather than solving access needs."
                    }
                  ],
                  "options": [
                    "Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry",
                    "Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk",
                    "Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access"
                  ],
                  "success": "Tradeoff record: programme-only supplier access protects privacy with an expiry owner; tested gate fallback supports availability within budget with an operations owner; named roles and supported recovery retain usability and accountability. Residual supplier failure and scope uncertainty remain explicit."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 1,
              "brief": "Defend the portal architecture and playbook with risk ownership, cost, privacy and usability. New evidence explains the initial login alert as maintenance; the public export remains independently confirmed.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Revise the misleading-alert hypothesis without ignoring separate exposure evidence.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-network\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"16\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"9\" y=\"2\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\"></rect><path d=\"M5 16v-3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h12a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3\"></path><path d=\"M12 12V8\"></path></svg><strong>Changed assurance scenario Â· simulation</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>New evidence</span><strong>Initial login alert was authorised maintenance</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Independent evidence</span><strong>Public export setting remains confirmed</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Decision</span><strong>Revise login hypothesis; contain and review separate exposure</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Owner / limit</span><strong>Service lead reviews scope; operations lead owns residual outage risk</strong></div></div><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">All evidence is false because the login alert was maintenance</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Accuse the account holder despite the correction</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Revise the login hypothesis, retain containment for the independently confirmed export and continue authorised scope review</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "All evidence is false because the login alert was maintenance",
                    "Accuse the account holder despite the correction",
                    "Revise the login hypothesis, retain containment for the independently confirmed export and continue authorised scope review"
                  ],
                  "answer": 2,
                  "feedback": "Separate evidence supports separate conclusions. Maintenance explains the login alert; it does not remove the confirmed public export. Correct the hypothesis without ignoring the exposure or accusing a person.",
                  "success": "Assurance revision: initial login alert explained by authorised maintenance; public export remains independently confirmed. Retain the justified access restriction, preserve records and have the incident lead review scope. No unsupported attribution is made."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Defend the portal architecture and playbook with risk ownership, cost, privacy and usability. New evidence explains the initial login alert as maintenance; the public export remains independently confirmed.",
              "eyebrow": "Portal design and incident lab",
              "prompt": "Defend a fresh supplier request and one residual risk in an individual viva.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"callout\">Fresh request: a new supplier wants all participant contacts to publish the programme faster. A limited budget remains, and the supplier promises it never fails.</div><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Keep programme-only access with expiry; decline unnecessary contacts, retain tested independent recovery and name the owner of remaining outage risk</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Grant the full export because the supplier promises reliability</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Use one shared organiser account to avoid assigning roles</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div><p class=\"micro\">Show your risk register, control locations, timeline, action log and recovery tests. Explain one alternative and remaining uncertainty. Your teacher reviews the individual viva; structured answers do not establish oral understanding or authorship.</p></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your system assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Keep programme-only access with expiry; decline unnecessary contacts, retain tested independent recovery and name the owner of remaining outage risk",
                    "Grant the full export because the supplier promises reliability",
                    "Use one shared organiser account to avoid assigning roles"
                  ],
                  "answer": 0,
                  "feedback": "The programme task still does not require contacts. A promise does not remove outage risk. Defend minimal scoped access, expiry, independent tested recovery and accountable ownership against the convenience claim.",
                  "success": "Individual defence outline: decline unnecessary contact export; retain programme-only access with expiry and a named owner; preserve tested independent recovery within budget. Residual supplier failure remains with the operations/service owner for review. Compare the convenience alternative and explain its privacy/accountability cost using the architecture, timeline and recovery evidence."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "The security assurance board",
            "concepts": [
              "Balance privacy, usability and cost",
              "Revise only the conclusion the new evidence changes",
              "Name residual risk, owner and review point; teacher reviews the viva"
            ],
            "question": "Maintenance explains a login alert, but a public export is independently confirmed. What changes?",
            "choices": [
              "Correct the login hypothesis while containing and reviewing the separate exposure",
              "Dismiss all evidence as false",
              "Accuse the account holder anyway"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "why": "One benign alert does not invalidate independent evidence of exposure. Update each conclusion according to its own supporting evidence."
          }
        }
