            {
              "line": 117,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Privacy versus supplier convenience"
            },
            {
              "line": 117,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep programme-only access; service owner reviews expiry"
            },
            {
              "line": 117,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Publishing a programme does not justify disclosing private contacts."
            },
            {
              "line": 118,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Availability versus limited budget"
            },
            {
              "line": 118,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fund the tested fallback; operations lead owns remaining outage risk"
            },
            {
              "line": 118,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A fallback supports continuity but cannot eliminate supplier failures."
            },
            {
              "line": 119,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Usability versus shared-account shortcuts"
            },
            {
              "line": 119,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Use named roles and supported recovery; lead reviews access"
            },
            {
              "line": 119,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A shared password hides accountability rather than solving access needs."
            },
            {
              "line": 122,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fictional portal: participants see their own registration, organisers manage entries, suppliers publish the programme. Map actors and trust boundaries; use the supplied risk estimates and name an owner."
            },
            {
              "line": 122,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Complete the Class 11 entry check."
            },
            {
              "line": 122,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Map assets, actors, boundaries and ownership."
            },
            {
              "line": 122,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Prioritise the three supplied risks with a responsible owner."
            },
            {
              "line": 123,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A browser, server, database and external provider have different jobs. DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport; neither grants record permission. This is a conceptual architecture, not a real deployment."
            },
            {
              "line": 123,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Assign each component its job."
            },
            {
              "line": 123,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Place the three controls at the boundary that owns them."
            },
            {
              "line": 123,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Defend the architectureâ€™s assumptions and limits."
            },
            {
              "line": 124,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Offline model only: no query, scanning, exploitation or live request is performed. Exercise amount rule: whole rupees from 0 to 5,000 inclusive. Server identity, authorisation, validation and structured data access remain distinct."
            },
            {
              "line": 124,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Match each misuse case to its missing control."
            },
            {
              "line": 124,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run the faulty model, enable the corrections and retest the same pack."
            },
            {
              "line": 124,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Test exact boundaries and an absent session."
            },
            {
              "line": 125,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The fictional supplier only publishes the programme. Budget: six exercise units. Meet the supplied requirements for limited access, managed secrets/trusted updates and independent recovery. Costs are invented, not vendor prices."
            },
            {
              "line": 125,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Allocate the six-unit budget to the required safeguards."
            },
            {
              "line": 125,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Write the minimum-access and expiry agreement."
            },
            {
              "line": 125,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Handle an outage when the supplier also holds a recovery route."
            },
            {
              "line": 126,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Synthetic evidence only. E2â€™s clock is known to run two minutes fast; other clocks are aligned. Gateway status 200 has unknown response bytes; a 403 belongs to a different path. Preserve raw times and avoid personal attribution."
            },
            {
              "line": 126,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Classify observed facts, hypotheses and missing evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 126,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Apply the supplied clock correction and inspect the ordered timeline."
            },
            {
              "line": 126,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State an alternative explanation and the evidence still needed."
            },
            {
              "line": 127,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Supplied inject: public export link confirmed; complete download scope unknown. Rehearse authorised roles and preserve evidence alongside urgent containment. The simulation sends no messages and changes no service."
            },
            {
              "line": 127,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Allocate the four incident roles."
            },
            {
              "line": 127,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Build the authorised action log in order."
            },
            {
              "line": 127,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose a factual stakeholder message without accusation or guarantees."
            },
            {
              "line": 128,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Incident 14:10; exercise targets: restore within 30 minutes and lose at most 10 minutes of data. Restore a harmless in-page dataset, test exact IDs/statuses and permissions, then record a limited recovery conclusion."
            },
            {
              "line": 128,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Interpret the recovery objectives and evidence requirement."
            },
            {
              "line": 128,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose a clean snapshot, restore the model and run four checks."
            },
            {
              "line": 128,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose an improvement that addresses the recovery dependency."
            },
            {
              "line": 129,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Defend the portal architecture and playbook with risk ownership, cost, privacy and usability. New evidence explains the initial login alert as maintenance; the public export remains independently confirmed."
            },
            {
              "line": 129,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Connect each tradeoff to a control and risk owner."
            },
            {
              "line": 129,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Revise the misleading-alert hypothesis without ignoring separate exposure evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 129,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Defend a fresh supplier request and one residual risk in an individual viva."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Asha maps the system risk"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Assets + actors + trust boundaries"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Authentication is not per-record permission"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Prioritise with supplied estimates; name an owner and remaining risk"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A supplier signs in but has no registration task. What access should the server allow?"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "All records because sign-in succeeded"
