            {
              "line": 23,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Entry check: session identity is authentication; permission for this action on this record is authorisation; exposed contacts create a confidentiality impact. Sign-in alone cannot authorise every record."
            },
            {
              "line": 24,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "System map: registration database is an asset; students, organisers and supplier are actors with different tasks; browser â†’ server crosses a trust boundary; registration lead plus weekly access review supplies ownership and a review point."
            },
            {
              "line": 25,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Exercise risk register: public export 9 â†’ registration lead first; single gate device 6 â†’ operations lead tests fallback second; editable poster 2 â†’ communications lead retains approved original third. Scores use supplied estimates, not precise real-world measurements; each owner reviews remaining risk."
            },
            {
              "line": 28,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Architecture roles: browser gathers/displays untrusted input; server enforces identity, permission and validation; database stays behind constrained service access; DNS locates a hostname and HTTPS protects transport without granting application permission."
            },
            {
              "line": 29,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Control locations: trusted session and per-record permission before private data access on the server; constrained service account and structured access at the database boundary; authentic expected payment status at the server/provider boundary using the providerâ€™s documented verification route."
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Assume HTTPS proves the operator is legitimate and every browser payment status is genuine"
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State that the diagram assumes a trusted server identity source and documented provider verification; HTTPS protects only the connection"
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Store database and provider secrets in the browser to reduce friction"
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A transport-protected connection does not establish operator legitimacy, a trusted role or payment proof. Keep server identity and provider verification assumptions explicit; no secret belongs in public client code."
            },
            {
              "line": 30,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Architecture defence: assumed trusted session source and documented provider verification must be implemented and tested. HTTPS protects the connection to the hostname; it does not certify the operator, authorise a record or prove a payment. This conceptual diagram is not assurance of a real service."
