              "line": 59,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Evidence timeline: E1 14:00 identity context; E2 corrected 14:01 sharing change (raw 14:03, known +2-minute clock); E3 and E4 14:02 on different paths. Raw records retained. Unknown bytes and session attribution remain unresolved; equal timestamps do not establish a causal order."
            },
            {
              "line": 59,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Only E2 has a supplied two-minute fast clock. Subtract two from its raw 14:03 time, keep raw values and do not invent corrections for other events."
            },
            {
              "line": 59,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 59,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Save evidence timeline"
            },
            {
              "line": 62,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Evidence ledger: logged gateway status is observed; full-file receipt is a hypothesis; the account holderâ€™s personal involvement is not established; response size and receiver are missing. Maintain uncertainty while authorised staff verify and contain risk."
            },
            {
              "line": 64,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The named account holder certainly stole every record"
            },
            {
              "line": 64,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Possible session misuse or path-specific denial remains an alternative; obtain request/response and access evidence without accusing a person"
            },
            {
              "line": 64,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A 403 on another path proves no exposure occurred anywhere"
            },
            {
              "line": 64,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The 403 concerns a different path, response bytes are unknown and a session does not establish its human operator. Retain alternatives and seek authorised evidence without accusation."
            },
            {
              "line": 64,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Alternative explanation: a session may have been misused, and the 403 may reflect a different protected path. Correlate authorised request, response-size and access evidence; do not equate a session label with personal attribution or dismiss exposure from an unrelated denial."
            },
            {
              "line": 67,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Role allocation: incident lead coordinates/authorises/escalates; authorised operator restricts and verifies exposure; recorder retains raw records and action times; communications lead sends approved factual updates. Students only rehearse these roles."
            },
            {
              "line": 68,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Action log: notify authorised lead and preserve available evidence; operator restricts exposure and verifies the restriction; confirm known scope and send an approved factual update; record times, reasons and owners before recovery handoff. Preserve records alongside urgent containment, not as a reason to delay it."
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "â€œA registration-export link was exposed and is now restricted. Scope is under review; use the approved contact for help. We will update you as facts are confirmed.â€"
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "â€œAsha stole every record. Share her name publicly.â€"
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "â€œNothing was received and no further action is needed; we have not checked.â€"
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Communicate the confirmed exposure and restriction, scope under review and approved help route. Do not attribute blame or guarantee no disclosure without evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Approved tabletop message: a registration-export link was exposed and is now restricted; scope is under review; use the approved help contact; further factual updates will follow. No person is accused and no unsupported no-disclosure guarantee is made. The exercise sends no message."
            },
            {
              "line": 72,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "recent-unsafe"
            },
            {
              "line": 76,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Exact expected IDs and statuses"
            },
            {
              "line": 76,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Organiser edit allowed; guest read denied"
            },
            {
              "line": 76,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Restore at 14:22: downtime 12 minutes â‰¤30"
            },
            {
              "line": 76,
              "kind": "Dynamic template",
              "text": "Snapshot ${c.clockLabel(snapshot.minute)}: data-loss window â‰¤10 minutes"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Snapshot to restore in the offline model"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "14:08 Â· most recent, incomplete, unsafe guest access"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "14:00 Â· four expected records, approved permissions"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Restore model and verify"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Dynamic template",
              "text": "${a.table} ${z.table}"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Restored synthetic data Â· expected R10 Confirmed, R20 Pending, R30 and R40 Confirmed"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Record"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Status"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Pass"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fail"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery record: clean 14:00 snapshot restores exact R10â€“R40 IDs/statuses; organiser edit works and guest read is denied. Restored at 14:22: 12-minute downtime and 10-minute data-loss window meet the supplied 30/10-minute objectives. Only these model checks are established; retain evidence and review residual risk."
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The recent copy fails completeness and guest-access checks. A newer timestamp and passing timing targets do not make it clean. Select the verified 14:00 point, restore again and rerun all four checks."
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "true"
            },
            {
              "line": 77,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Save recovery test"
            },
            {
              "line": 80,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery objectives: time objective limits exercise downtime to 30 minutes; point objective limits data-loss window to 10 minutes. Copy completion alone is insufficient; test exact data and intended access before reopening. These are supplied planning targets, not universal deadlines."
            },
            {
              "line": 82,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep the only recovery key with the supplier that just failed"
            },
            {
              "line": 82,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep an independently available recovery method, schedule a restoration/access test and assign an owner to review the result"
            },
            {
              "line": 82,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Skip access tests next time because the copy command worked"
            },
            {
              "line": 82,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Recovery depends on accessible private recovery methods and repeated data/access tests with a responsible owner. Copy success or supplier dependence leaves the same weakness in place."
            },
            {
              "line": 82,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Improvement: retain an independent private recovery route; schedule a harmless restoration test covering exact data and permissions; assign the operations lead a review date and follow up failures. A successful small exercise cannot guarantee every real incident outcome."
            },
            {
              "line": 85,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Tradeoff record: programme-only supplier access protects privacy with an expiry owner; tested gate fallback supports availability within budget with an operations owner; named roles and supported recovery retain usability and accountability. Residual supplier failure and scope uncertainty remain explicit."
            },
            {
              "line": 86,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "All evidence is false because the login alert was maintenance"
            },
            {
              "line": 86,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Accuse the account holder despite the correction"
            },
            {
              "line": 86,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Revise the login hypothesis, retain containment for the independently confirmed export and continue authorised scope review"
            },
            {
              "line": 86,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Separate evidence supports separate conclusions. Maintenance explains the login alert; it does not remove the confirmed public export. Correct the hypothesis without ignoring the exposure or accusing a person."
            },
            {
              "line": 86,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Assurance revision: initial login alert explained by authorised maintenance; public export remains independently confirmed. Retain the justified access restriction, preserve records and have the incident lead review scope. No unsupported attribution is made."
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Fresh request: a new supplier wants all participant contacts to publish the programme faster. A limited budget remains, and the supplier promises it never fails."
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep programme-only access with expiry; decline unnecessary contacts, retain tested independent recovery and name the owner of remaining outage risk"
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Grant the full export because the supplier promises reliability"
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Use one shared organiser account to avoid assigning roles"
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The programme task still does not require contacts. A promise does not remove outage risk. Defend minimal scoped access, expiry, independent tested recovery and accountable ownership against the convenience claim."
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Individual defence outline: decline unnecessary contact export; retain programme-only access with expiry and a named owner; preserve tested independent recovery within budget. Residual supplier failure remains with the operations/service owner for review. Compare the convenience alternative and explain its privacy/accountability cost using the architecture, timeline and recovery evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 87,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Show your risk register, control locations, timeline, action log and recovery tests. Explain one alternative and remaining uncertainty. Your teacher reviews the individual viva; structured answers do not establish oral understanding or authorship."
            },
            {
              "line": 101,
              "kind": "Dynamic template",
              "text": "evidence-${slug}"
            },
            {
              "line": 103,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "object"
            },
            {
              "line": 108,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "from-personal-safety-to-system-risk"
            },
            {
              "line": 108,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "the-breach-tabletop"
            },
            {
              "line": 109,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Portal design and incident lab"
            },
            {
              "line": 109,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "lab"
            },
            {
              "line": 110,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Your system assurance record"
            },
            {
              "line": 110,
              "kind": "On-screen text",
              "text": "Use this checked evidence alongside the earlier portal, timeline and recovery chapter records for your individual explanation. Your teacher reviews the viva separately. All tests use fictional offline models."
            },
