              "eyebrow": "AI evidence and assurance lab",
              "prompt": "Bound the claim by this tiny prepared pack.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">All dim inputs always fail</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">These six illustrative inputs show changed or review outputs; collect separate relevant shift evidence and retain human review</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Two bright examples prove robustness in every condition</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your AI assurance record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use this checked record with the moduleâ€™s baseline, manifest, calculations and model card for your teacherâ€™s individual review. Automatic checks assess structured decisions, not authorship or the oral defence. All results are prepared classroom evidence.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "All dim inputs always fail",
                    "These six illustrative inputs show changed or review outputs; collect separate relevant shift evidence and retain human review",
                    "Two bright examples prove robustness in every condition"
                  ],
                  "answer": 1,
                  "feedback": "Two objects and three illustrative views are not a population study or a measured deployed model. Report counts, separate abstention from wrong labels and keep the claim narrow.",
                  "success": "Shift-test limit: bright 2/2 correct; dim 1/2 correct; crop 0/2 correct with one review and one wrong label in this prepared pack. No live model was measured. Collect separate relevant examples and retain human review before claiming broader performance."
                }
              ]
