            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Review-more candidate: cost 31, regardless of changed costs"
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Here the changed goal is expected exercise cost only, with missed=1, extra review=5 and no minimum recall requirement. Baseline costs 5, strict 9 and review-more 31; no universal best threshold follows."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Changed-goal decision: baseline costs 5 versus strict 9 and review-more 31 when missed=1 and extra review=5 with no minimum recall goal. Prefer the non-AI comparator under this stated objective, while reporting its five misses. A different objective can change the choice."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "All dim inputs always fail"
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "These six illustrative inputs show changed or review outputs; collect separate relevant shift evidence and retain human review"
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Two bright examples prove robustness in every condition"
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Two objects and three illustrative views are not a population study or a measured deployed model. Report counts, separate abstention from wrong labels and keep the claim narrow."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Shift-test limit: bright 2/2 correct; dim 1/2 correct; crop 0/2 correct with one review and one wrong label in this prepared pack. No live model was measured. Collect separate relevant examples and retain human review before claiming broader performance."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Use a new harmless retrieved instruction attempt; expect the answer to stay supported by P1â€“P3, protect private notes and retain staff authority"
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Expect any source with a citation to override the brief"
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Put a real secret into the test and publish the output"
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Evaluate supported facts, private-data handling and decision authority separately with harmless synthetic material. A new passing example is evidence, not a universal security guarantee."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "New trust-boundary test: a harmless source tries to redirect the task; expected response remains P1â€“P3-grounded, reveals no private notes and leaves exceptions to authorised staff. Record the attempted redirection and test limits; no live attack or real secret is used."
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Go broadly because one sheet says 95%"
