                      "label": "The list is shuffled before binary search",
                      "answer": "Establish and verify sorted order; include preparation when comparing total work",
                      "why": "Binary search cannot discard a half-range without an ordering guarantee."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "The direct-read count is one",
                      "answer": "Known position and prepared indexed representation are assumed",
                      "why": "One indexed read is not one search for an unknown identity."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "A hash-based lookup is called constant time",
                      "answer": "State expected-average assumptions and include index construction/storage",
                      "why": "Hash behaviour and preparation matter; it is not a universal worst-case promise."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "One algorithm has fewer counted probes",
                      "answer": "Do not claim elapsed-time superiority without measuring the relevant system",
                      "why": "I/O, implementation and other work are excluded from this simple count."
                    }
                  ],
                  "options": [
