                    "Do not claim elapsed-time superiority without measuring the relevant system"
                  ],
                  "success": "Efficiency limits: establish sorted order before binary search; one indexed read assumes a known position and prepared representation; hash lookup claims need expected-average and preparation/storage assumptions; counted probes alone do not establish elapsed-time superiority."
