              "caption": "Kabir designs an offline workflow for synthetic service-alert records. Each record has a stable ID, category and priority score from zero to one hundred. The exercise routes scores at least seventy to human review; lower valid scores are recorded only.",
              "dialogue": "A pipeline needs clear contracts between steps.",
              "status": "Inspect the workflow",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 17.365,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/ct-alerts-pipeline.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-workflow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"13\" y=\"13\" rx=\"2\"></rect></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 reliable automation lab</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Build a reliable alerts pipeline</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/ct-alerts-pipeline.webp\" alt=\"Students arrange input, validation, processing and output trays, with a separate invalid-record review tray and a preserved original folder.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>A reliable workflow records valid outputs, quarantined inputs and unfinished work without hiding the original evidence.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models only. No real registrations, notifications, messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "build-a-reliable-alerts-pipeline-2",
              "label": "The problem",
              "title": "Not every input is valid",
              "mood": "surprise",
              "caption": "The pack includes an out-of-range score and an unknown category. Silently dropping those rows would make the output look complete while hiding lost evidence. The original batch must remain available for review and repair.",
              "dialogue": "Invalid input needs a visible route.",
              "status": "Risk unresolved",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 18.015,
              "duration": 14.336,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-workflow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"13\" y=\"13\" rx=\"2\"></rect></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 reliable automation lab</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Not every input is valid</h2><figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption>Offline alerts pipeline Â· explicit contracts at every handoff</figcaption><ol><li><div><strong>Input</strong><span>Preserve original batch</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Validate</strong><span>Schema, stable IDs and conflict checks</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Transform</strong><span>Apply the stated review threshold</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Output</strong><span>Ledger, quarantine and checkpoint log</span></div></li></ol><p>Invalid or conflicting input is quarantined with a reason. An output fault stops with completed IDs and pending work preserved. This diagram sends no alerts.</p></figure><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models only. No real registrations, notifications, messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "build-a-reliable-alerts-pipeline-3",
              "label": "How it works",
              "title": "Four connected stages",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "Preserve the original input, validate the schema and stable IDs, transform valid records, then commit a retry-safe output ledger and action log. Quarantine malformed or conflicting records without inventing values or overwriting originals.",
              "dialogue": "Each stage states what it receives and produces.",
              "status": "Build the contract",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 33.001,
              "duration": 16.768,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-workflow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"13\" y=\"13\" rx=\"2\"></rect></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 reliable automation lab</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Four connected stages</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Preserve input â†’ validate/quarantine â†’ transform â†’ ledger/log</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Score â‰¥70 is the invented review boundary</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Keep invalid/conflicting input visible; no external output</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models only. No real registrations, notifications, messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "build-a-reliable-alerts-pipeline-4",
              "label": "Your decision",
              "title": "Choose the invalid-record path",
              "mood": "thinking",
              "caption": "Should an invalid score be silently changed to zero, deleted from the evidence, or held in a labelled quarantine while valid records follow the stated contract?",
              "dialogue": "A convenient output must not hide an invalid input.",
              "status": "Decision required",
              "tone": "trouble",
              "start": 50.419,
              "duration": 10.517,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-workflow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"13\" y=\"13\" rx=\"2\"></rect></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 reliable automation lab</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Choose the invalid-record path</h2><figure class=\"diagram\"><figcaption>Offline alerts pipeline Â· explicit contracts at every handoff</figcaption><ol><li><div><strong>Input</strong><span>Preserve original batch</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Validate</strong><span>Schema, stable IDs and conflict checks</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Transform</strong><span>Apply the stated review threshold</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></li><li><div><strong>Output</strong><span>Ledger, quarantine and checkpoint log</span></div></li></ol><p>Invalid or conflicting input is quarantined with a reason. An output fault stops with completed IDs and pending work preserved. This diagram sends no alerts.</p></figure><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"storyQuestion\"><strong>What should happen to an invalid score?</strong></p><div class=\"actionBank\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Change it silently to zero</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Delete the source row</button><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Quarantine with a reason while preserving the original</button></div><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\">Test my decision</button></div><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models only. No real registrations, notifications, messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
