            {
              "id": "do-not-confuse-a-pattern-with-a-cause-1",
              "label": "Meet the team",
              "title": "A misleading alert comparison",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Kabir sees a summary claiming that alerts increased from twenty to thirty, so the new rule caused a deterioration. The two windows differ in duration and number of observed readings. Some readings are missing in the second window.",
              "dialogue": "A raw count needs a denominator and a time window.",
              "status": "Inspect the workflow",
              "tone": "normal",
              "start": 0,
              "duration": 14.485,
              "html": "<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"image\" href=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/ct-alerts-pipeline.webp\"/><div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-workflow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\" x=\"13\" y=\"13\" rx=\"2\"></rect></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 reliable automation lab</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">A misleading alert comparison</h2><figure class=\"sceneIllustration\"><img src=\"/cyber-missions/class-12/ct-alerts-pipeline.webp\" alt=\"Students arrange input, validation, processing and output trays, with a separate invalid-record review tray and a preserved original folder.\" width=\"1400\" height=\"788\" decoding=\"async\"/><figcaption>A reliable workflow records valid outputs, quarantined inputs and unfinished work without hiding the original evidence.</figcaption></figure><small class=\"note\">Synthetic records and offline models only. No real registrations, notifications, messages or service changes.</small></div>"
            },
            {
