              "eyebrow": "Reliable automation lab",
              "prompt": "Replace a misleading raw-count summary with a labelled comparison.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">Misleading claim to audit: â€œ30 alerts versus 20 proves the new rule caused deterioration.â€ Build the requested observed-rate comparison while retaining windows and missingness. Counts can be useful, but they do not answer this rate question alone.</p><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Comparison measure</span><select><option value=\"counts\" selected=\"\">Raw flagged totals only</option><option value=\"rate\">Flagged / observed readings, with time windows</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Missing-reading treatment</span><select><option value=\"normal\" selected=\"\">Assume missing readings were normal</option><option value=\"unknown\">Keep missing outcomes unknown and report their count</option></select></label><button class=\"secondary\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Build comparison table</button><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Save corrected comparison</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your automation evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the checked records across the module for your teacherâ€™s individual review. Automatic checks assess structured decisions, not authorship or the oral defence. All traces are fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Window A: 1h, 100 observed, 20 flagged, 0 missing. Window B: 3h, 300 observed, 30 flagged, 15 missing. Compare observed rates with denominators/time windows; missing readings are not known negatives.",
              "eyebrow": "Reliable automation lab",
              "prompt": "Interpret the difference without an unsupported causal claim.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">The new rule definitely caused the count increase</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">B has a lower observed rate in this pack, but different windows/workloads and missingness leave alternative explanations; seek comparable evidence before a causal claim</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Treat the 15 missing readings as known normal readings</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your automation evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the checked records across the module for your teacherâ€™s individual review. Automatic checks assess structured decisions, not authorship or the oral defence. All traces are fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "The new rule definitely caused the count increase",
                    "B has a lower observed rate in this pack, but different windows/workloads and missingness leave alternative explanations; seek comparable evidence before a causal claim",
                    "Treat the 15 missing readings as known normal readings"
                  ],
                  "answer": 1,
                  "feedback": "Observed rates are 20/100 and 30/300; windows differ and 15 readings are missing in B. Those observations do not isolate a cause.",
                  "success": "Cautious interpretation: A observed flag rate 20%, B 10%; windows are 1h and 3h, with 15 missing readings in B. Workload mix, window length and missingness are alternatives to investigate; no controlled evidence establishes a causal effect of the rule."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "Kabir checks the denominator",
            "concepts": [
              "A: 20/100 observed readings; B: 30/300",
              "Windows 1h/3h; B has 15 missing readings",
              "A rate difference alone does not establish a cause"
            ],
            "question": "What causal conclusion follows from these two windows?",
            "choices": [
              "The new rule definitely caused deterioration",
              "None yet; different workloads, windows and missingness leave alternatives",
              "Missing readings are all normal"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "The observed rates differ, but the comparison does not isolate a cause. Keep the windows, denominators and unknown readings visible."
          }
        },
