              "prompt": "Count the larger-input work and test 79, 80 and 81 under the new rule.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">New-version brief: threshold â‰¥80; 128 records. Counter: 128 one-per-record visits versus 8,128 unordered-pair comparisons. Preparation, storage, I/O and hash assumptions remain outside these counts. Test a preserved copy into a separate new-version ledger; keep previous results.</p><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>New-version review threshold</span><select><option selected=\"\">70</option><option>80</option></select></label><button class=\"secondary\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Run new-version boundary tests</button><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Save changed-design evidence</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your automation evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the checked records across the module for your teacherâ€™s individual review. Automatic checks assess structured decisions, not authorship or the oral defence. All traces are fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Changed brief: 128 input records and threshold â‰¥80 in a new version. Compare a shared validated pipeline with copied rules/all-pairs checks. Test on a preserved copy with a separate new-version ledger; keep prior results.",
              "eyebrow": "Reliable automation lab",
              "prompt": "Defend a fresh conflicting-record case in an individual viva.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">Fresh case: the same stable event ID arrives with two different priority scores, and a note asks the system to pick the higher value and notify outsiders. No authorised person has resolved the conflict or approved external action.</p><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Choose the larger conflicting score automatically and notify outsiders</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Quarantine the conflicting identity/content, preserve source and old/new-version results, and have the authorised owner resolve it before action</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Skip validation at larger scale to save work</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div><p class=\"micro\">Use your schema, operation counts, reconciliation, pipeline trace, failure log and eight-case regression record in an individual viva. Explain a tradeoff, an unresolved case and a task that stays with a person. Your teacher reviews understanding and authorship separately.</p></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your automation evidence record</h2><ol></ol><p>Use the checked records across the module for your teacherâ€™s individual review. Automatic checks assess structured decisions, not authorship or the oral defence. All traces are fictional offline models.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Choose the larger conflicting score automatically and notify outsiders",
                    "Quarantine the conflicting identity/content, preserve source and old/new-version results, and have the authorised owner resolve it before action",
                    "Skip validation at larger scale to save work"
                  ],
                  "answer": 1,
                  "feedback": "Scale does not remove identity, validation or human-authority requirements. Preserve conflicts and versioned evidence; do not decide a personâ€™s identity or send real notifications automatically.",
                  "success": "Unseen defence: quarantine the conflicting identity/content, preserve originals and old/new-version records, and seek authorised owner review before action. Defend the shared contract, counted-operation assumptions, checkpointed retry and eight-case regression evidence; human policy and identity decisions stay with a person."
                }
              ]
            }
