            {
              "line": 166,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Correctness"
            },
            {
              "line": 166,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Shared validated contracts with invalid, conflict and retry paths"
            },
            {
              "line": 166,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "An efficient design must still preserve required behaviour and evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 167,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Efficiency"
            },
            {
              "line": 167,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Measure stated operations; include preparation, storage and implementation assumptions"
            },
            {
              "line": 167,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Counts of probes or pairs are not complete elapsed-time measurements."
            },
            {
              "line": 168,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Maintainability"
            },
            {
              "line": 168,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "One shared rule, versioned results and old plus new regression tests"
            },
            {
              "line": 168,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Conflicting copies of a rule make future changes harder to verify."
            },
            {
              "line": 169,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Human authority"
            },
            {
              "line": 169,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Authorised owner reviews identity conflicts and approves policy changes"
            },
            {
              "line": 169,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Automation does not decide which person is correct or authorise a new policy."
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Merge every Riya row because names match"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Preserve stable IDs and original rows; hold conflicts/unmatched references for authorised review and retest the repaired relationship"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Keep the last conflicting value and delete the earlier evidence"
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Names are not unique identity keys. Preserve conflicting and unmatched evidence; a missing check-in is unknown, not proof of absence."
            },
            {
              "line": 172,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Reconciliation decision: keep R02 and R03 distinct; preserve original rows and the unresolved R01/R02/R05 cases, seek authorised corrections and retest key uniqueness/reference coverage. R03 attendance remains unknown without check-in evidence."
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Overwrite committed A01 score 70 with the new score 5"
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Delete the source batch so the conflict disappears"
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Quarantine the changed A01 payload, preserve prior output and both source versions, and seek authorised review"
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Retry safety applies to identical content. Different content under an existing ID is a conflict, not permission to overwrite history."
            },
            {
              "line": 173,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Conflict handling: changed content under A01 is quarantined for authorised review; prior output and both source versions remain. Do not silently overwrite a committed event or treat a changed payload as an identical retry."
            },
            {
              "line": 174,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The new rule definitely caused the count increase"
            },
            {
              "line": 174,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "B has a lower observed rate in this pack, but different windows/workloads and missingness leave alternative explanations; seek comparable evidence before a causal claim"
            },
            {
              "line": 174,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Treat the 15 missing readings as known normal readings"
            },
            {
              "line": 174,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Observed rates are 20/100 and 30/300; windows differ and 15 readings are missing in B. Those observations do not isolate a cause."
            },
            {
              "line": 174,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Cautious interpretation: A observed flag rate 20%, B 10%; windows are 1h and 3h, with 15 missing readings in B. Workload mix, window length and missingness are alternatives to investigate; no controlled evidence establishes a causal effect of the rule."
            },
            {
              "line": 175,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "A valid new capacity score exactly 70 â†’ Review; missing score â†’ quarantine; preserve both as regression cases"
            },
            {
              "line": 175,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Change expected exact-70 output to Record only to match the bug"
            },
            {
              "line": 175,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Remove all invalid-input cases after adding capacity"
            },
            {
              "line": 175,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "The inclusive â‰¥70 contract applies to the new supported category too. Missing is not zero; retain old and new cases instead of editing expectations to hide a regression."
            },
            {
              "line": 175,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fresh regression evidence: supported capacity at exactly 70 requests Review; an absent score is quarantined, never invented as zero. Add both cases while retaining the original eight-case pack; finite passing examples do not prove all possible inputs."
            },
            {
              "line": 176,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose the larger conflicting score automatically and notify outsiders"
            },
            {
              "line": 176,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Quarantine the conflicting identity/content, preserve source and old/new-version results, and have the authorised owner resolve it before action"
            },
            {
              "line": 176,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Skip validation at larger scale to save work"
            },
            {
              "line": 176,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Scale does not remove identity, validation or human-authority requirements. Preserve conflicts and versioned evidence; do not decide a personâ€™s identity or send real notifications automatically."
            },
            {
              "line": 176,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Unseen defence: quarantine the conflicting identity/content, preserve originals and old/new-version records, and seek authorised owner review before action. Defend the shared contract, counted-operation assumptions, checkpointed retry and eight-case regression evidence; human policy and identity decisions stay with a person."
            },
            {
              "line": 179,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Fictional registration desk: stable-ID lookup, ordered programme, undo history and first-come support. Choose a structure by its operation. The demo traces abstract removal order, not a performance benchmark."
            },
            {
              "line": 179,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Match the four operations to their data structures."
            },
            {
              "line": 179,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Predict and run one stack removal and one queue removal."
            },
            {
              "line": 179,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State stable-identity and human-policy limits."
            },
            {
              "line": 180,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Count one indexed access, one record probe or one unordered-pair comparison as specified. Binary search uses an already sorted list and searches for the last item; preparation and wall-clock costs are excluded."
            },
            {
              "line": 180,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Identify constant, logarithmic, linear and quadratic growth."
            },
            {
              "line": 180,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run counts for 8, 16 and 32 records and record the observed values."
            },
            {
              "line": 180,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State the assumptions behind the efficiency claim."
            },
            {
              "line": 181,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Synthetic dirty tables: one expected check-in per registration. Stable IDs link tables; names are not unique. Preserve repeated/conflicting rows and unmatched references; no check-in record means attendance unknown."
            },
            {
              "line": 181,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Specify primary-key and foreign-key relationships."
            },
            {
              "line": 181,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run stable-ID reconciliation and classify every result."
            },
            {
              "line": 181,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose an evidence-preserving correction and human handoff."
            },
            {
              "line": 182,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Offline synthetic alerts: ID A plus two digits, category latency/outage, finite priority score 0â€“100. Exercise rule: score â‰¥70 â†’ human Review, otherwise Record only. Keep originals, quarantine and a retry-safe ledger; no messages are sent."
            },
            {
              "line": 182,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Arrange the four pipeline stages."
            },
            {
              "line": 182,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Define the contracts between input, validation, transformation and output."
            },
            {
              "line": 182,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run mixed valid/invalid inputs and preserve the unresolved records."
            },
            {
              "line": 183,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Rehearse empty input, malformed records, identical repeats and partial output failure. Stop with a checkpoint on output failure and retry only after its cause is resolved. Conflicting event content requires review."
            },
            {
              "line": 183,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Map each fault to a visible safe response."
            },
            {
              "line": 183,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run a prepared partial failure, then retry the preserved batch."
            },
            {
              "line": 183,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Handle changed content arriving under an already committed ID."
            },
            {
              "line": 184,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Window A: 1h, 100 observed, 20 flagged, 0 missing. Window B: 3h, 300 observed, 30 flagged, 15 missing. Compare observed rates with denominators/time windows; missing readings are not known negatives."
            },
            {
              "line": 184,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Calculate flag rates using observed-reading denominators."
            },
            {
              "line": 184,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Replace a misleading raw-count summary with a labelled comparison."
            },
            {
              "line": 184,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Interpret the difference without an unsupported causal claim."
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "New requirement: support capacity alerts while retaining latency/outage, validation, quarantine and retry handling. Review still means score â‰¥70. The draft introduces a deliberate >70 regression; preserve old expectations and run eight old/new cases."
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Write expected outcomes for the minimum eight-case pack."
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run the draft, repair the regression and rerun all eight cases."
            },
            {
              "line": 185,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Transfer the inclusive rule to a fresh capacity/missing-score pair."
            },
            {
              "line": 186,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Changed brief: 128 input records and threshold â‰¥80 in a new version. Compare a shared validated pipeline with copied rules/all-pairs checks. Test on a preserved copy with a separate new-version ledger; keep prior results."
            },
            {
              "line": 186,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Compare correctness, efficiency, maintainability and human oversight."
            },
            {
              "line": 186,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Count the larger-input work and test 79, 80 and 81 under the new rule."
