            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Synthetic same-day whole-rupee transfers only. Transparent review rule: an intermediary forwards 90â€“100% of an incoming amount within five minutes. This describes a pattern, not intent or guilt. Independent receipt RP1 explains Câ€™s group purchase; Vâ€™s source/purpose remain unresolved.",
              "eyebrow": "Private evidence and response lab",
              "prompt": "State a cautious conclusion without accusing an account holder.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Two pattern flags prove two criminals</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">One benign receipt proves every other path is safe</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Two flags include one documented benign match and one unresolved path; keep evidence gaps and avoid attribution or a meaningful accuracy claim from unknown labels</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your prevention and response case file</h2><ol></ol><p>Structured decisions are checked automatically. Your teacher reviews the actual case dossier, team briefing, individual defence and reflection. All records are fictional; no real contact, transfer or report occurs.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "Two pattern flags prove two criminals",
                    "One benign receipt proves every other path is safe",
                    "Two flags include one documented benign match and one unresolved path; keep evidence gaps and avoid attribution or a meaningful accuracy claim from unknown labels"
                  ],
                  "answer": 2,
                  "feedback": "The flag describes time/amount/route, not intent. C has supplied benign context, V remains unresolved, and unknown truth labels cannot support a reliable accuracy or guilt claim.",
                  "success": "Pattern conclusion: two flagged intermediaries, C with documented benign purchase context and V unresolved. If used as a fraud verdict, the benign match would be a false accusation. Keep flags private for authorised review; no intent, guilt, precision or false-positive rate is established from these incomplete labels."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "Asha tests the transaction hypothesis",
            "concepts": [
              "A pattern flag does not establish intent",
              "Test independent benign context and missing evidence",
              "Unknown truth labels do not support an accuracy or guilt claim"
            ],
            "question": "The rule flags V and a documented group collector C. What can be concluded?",
            "choices": [
              "Both account holders are criminals",
              "One receipt proves every path safe",
              "There are two review patterns; retain Câ€™s benign context and Vâ€™s unresolved evidence gaps"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "why": "The rule describes time, amount and route. C has a supplied innocent explanation, V remains unresolved, and no public allegation is supported."
          }
