              "start": 59.112,
              "duration": 15.552,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-folder-search\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10.7 20H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.9a2 2 0 0 1 1.69.9l.81 1.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.67.9H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4.1\"></path><path d=\"m21 21-1.9-1.9\"></path><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"17\" r=\"3\"></circle></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 private casework desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">A tested revision</h2><div class=\"artifact\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-folder-search\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10.7 20H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.9a2 2 0 0 1 1.69.9l.81 1.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.67.9H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4.1\"></path><path d=\"m21 21-1.9-1.9\"></path><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"17\" r=\"3\"></circle></svg><strong>Prevention-aid test brief Â· fictional case</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Draft</span><strong>Trust familiar display name; approve first; wait for perfect file; forward screenshots</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>P1 Â· before payment</span><strong>Pause and use a previously known independent route</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>P2 Â· after suspected loss</span><strong>Prompt trusted bank/adult/official help; restricted evidence</strong></div><div class=\"artifactRow\"><span>Required record</span><strong>Test before and after revision; peer/teacher reviews usability</strong></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records only. No real transfer, identity upload, external contact, report submission or allegation.</small></div>"
            },
            {
              "id": "design-prevention-that-can-be-tested-6",
              "label": "Enter the lab",
              "title": "Enter the prevention lab",
              "mood": "happy",
              "caption": "Match controls to failure modes, run and revise the two-case aid, then handle an unanswered verification call. Your teacher or peer reviews actual usability separately from the structured check.",
              "dialogue": "Make the next safe action easy to identify.",
              "status": "Ready for practice",
              "tone": "resolved",
              "start": 75.314,
              "duration": 12.928,
              "html": "<div class=\"storyBoard\"><div class=\"appBar\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-folder-search\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10.7 20H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.9a2 2 0 0 1 1.69.9l.81 1.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.67.9H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4.1\"></path><path d=\"m21 21-1.9-1.9\"></path><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"17\" r=\"3\"></circle></svg><strong>Cyberpur Â· Class 12 private casework desk</strong></div><h2 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Enter the prevention lab</h2><div class=\"storyFacts\"><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Define expected safe outcomes for two cases</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Replace appearance-based checking and delayed help</span></div><div class=\"storyFact\" data-active=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg><span>Preserve before/after results; peer/teacher reviews real usability</span></div></div><small class=\"note\">Fictional records only. No real transfer, identity upload, external contact, report submission or allegation.</small></div>"
            }
          ],
          "practice": [
            {
              "stage": 0,
              "brief": "Prototype a verification aid, test two fictional situations and retain a before/after revision log. Pre-payment verification and after-loss help require different routes. Passing two prepared cases is limited evidence; a peer/teacher reviews usability under pressure separately.",
              "eyebrow": "Private evidence and response lab",
              "prompt": "Match safeguards to specific failure modes.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Caller chooses the only verification number</span><select aria-label=\"Caller chooses the only verification number\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Use a previously known independent contact route</option><option>Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting, without waiting for a perfect file</option><option>Restrict originals and redact the classroom copy</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Suspected financial cyber-fraud loss has already occurred</span><select aria-label=\"Suspected financial cyber-fraud loss has already occurred\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Use a previously known independent contact route</option><option>Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting, without waiting for a perfect file</option><option>Restrict originals and redact the classroom copy</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Private evidence is proposed for class-group forwarding</span><select aria-label=\"Private evidence is proposed for class-group forwarding\"><option value=\"\" selected=\"\">Chooseâ€¦</option><option>Use a previously known independent contact route</option><option>Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting, without waiting for a perfect file</option><option>Restrict originals and redact the classroom copy</option></select></label><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check my map</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your prevention and response case file</h2><ol></ol><p>Structured decisions are checked automatically. Your teacher reviews the actual case dossier, team briefing, individual defence and reflection. All records are fictional; no real contact, transfer or report occurs.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "MatchTable",
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "label": "Caller chooses the only verification number",
                      "answer": "Use a previously known independent contact route",
                      "why": "The claimant must not control its own verifier."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Suspected financial cyber-fraud loss has already occurred",
                      "answer": "Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting, without waiting for a perfect file",
                      "why": "An after-loss aid must not delay urgent contact while gathering evidence."
                    },
                    {
                      "label": "Private evidence is proposed for class-group forwarding",
                      "answer": "Restrict originals and redact the classroom copy",
                      "why": "Help-seeking should not create another disclosure."
                    }
                  ],
                  "options": [
                    "Use a previously known independent contact route",
                    "Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting, without waiting for a perfect file",
                    "Restrict originals and redact the classroom copy"
                  ],
                  "success": "Prevention map: caller-controlled verifier â†’ previously known independent contact; after-loss delay â†’ prompt trusted bank/adult/official help; group forwarding â†’ restricted originals and redacted classroom copy. Each safeguard addresses a specific failure mode."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "stage": 1,
              "brief": "Prototype a verification aid, test two fictional situations and retain a before/after revision log. Pre-payment verification and after-loss help require different routes. Passing two prepared cases is limited evidence; a peer/teacher reviews usability under pressure separately.",
              "eyebrow": "Private evidence and response lab",
              "prompt": "Test the weak draft, revise it and rerun both cases.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><p class=\"callout\">Run the supplied weak draft before editing. P1 requires independent verification before payment; P2 requires prompt trusted help with restricted evidence. Preserve the first results and retest your revision. This structured simulation does not measure actual peer usability under pressure.</p><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Verification route in the aid</span><select disabled=\"\"><option value=\"appearance\" selected=\"\">Trust a familiar display name or caller-supplied number</option><option value=\"independent\">Use a previously known independent contact route</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Before an unverified payment</span><select disabled=\"\"><option value=\"approve\" selected=\"\">Approve first and verify later</option><option value=\"pause\">Pause money/secrets until the exact request is independently checked</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>After a suspected financial cyber-fraud loss</span><select disabled=\"\"><option value=\"wait\" selected=\"\">Wait for every screenshot before asking for help</option><option value=\"prompt\">Prompt trusted bank/adult/official reporting without waiting for a perfect file</option></select></label><label class=\"matchRow\"><span>Private evidence handling</span><select disabled=\"\"><option value=\"public\" selected=\"\">Forward private screenshots to groups</option><option value=\"restricted\">Restrict originals; redact classroom copies; share only with authorised helpers</option></select></label><button class=\"secondary\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3\"></polygon></svg>Test aid on both cases</button><button class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Save tested prevention aid</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your prevention and response case file</h2><ol></ol><p>Structured decisions are checked automatically. Your teacher reviews the actual case dossier, team briefing, individual defence and reflection. All records are fictional; no real contact, transfer or report occurs.</p></div>",
              "interactions": []
            },
            {
              "stage": 2,
              "brief": "Prototype a verification aid, test two fictional situations and retain a before/after revision log. Pre-payment verification and after-loss help require different routes. Passing two prepared cases is limited evidence; a peer/teacher reviews usability under pressure separately.",
              "eyebrow": "Private evidence and response lab",
              "prompt": "Handle an unanswered independent verification attempt.",
              "html": "<section><div class=\"lab senior\"><div class=\"senior\"><div class=\"board\"><div class=\"actionBank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A known contact does not answer: keep the request unverified and do not pay; use another previously known route/trusted adult. If loss already occurred, do not delay bank/official help.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A failed callback proves the callerâ€™s emergency and authorises payment</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"choice\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Use the new number the suspicious caller just supplied</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" disabled=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>Check decision</button></div></div></div></section>",
              "evidence": "<div class=\"evidence\"><h2>Your prevention and response case file</h2><ol></ol><p>Structured decisions are checked automatically. Your teacher reviews the actual case dossier, team briefing, individual defence and reflection. All records are fictional; no real contact, transfer or report occurs.</p></div>",
              "interactions": [
                {
                  "type": "ChoiceTask",
                  "choices": [
                    "A known contact does not answer: keep the request unverified and do not pay; use another previously known route/trusted adult. If loss already occurred, do not delay bank/official help.",
                    "A failed callback proves the callerâ€™s emergency and authorises payment",
                    "Use the new number the suspicious caller just supplied"
                  ],
                  "answer": 0,
                  "feedback": "An unanswered check is not confirmation. Keep the pre-payment claim paused while using an independent alternative; an after-loss response should still seek prompt help.",
                  "success": "Aid transfer: no answer leaves the request unresolved, so no payment or secret disclosure is authorised. Use another previously known independent route and trusted-adult support. A real loss still requires prompt bank/official help without waiting for that callback."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "decisionTask": {
            "title": "Kabir tests the prevention aid",
            "concepts": [
              "Define expected safe outcomes for two cases",
              "Replace appearance-based checking and delayed help",
              "Preserve before/after results; peer/teacher reviews real usability"
            ],
            "question": "The weak guide fails both cases. What should Kabir do?",
            "choices": [
              "Name the independent route, prompt help and restricted evidence handling; rerun both cases",
              "Delete the failed case",
              "Keep the instructions and improve only the colours"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "why": "Revise the unsafe/ambiguous steps and retain the before/after evidence. Appearance does not repair a failed verification rule."
          }
        },
