              "text": "Build a verification protocol outside the suspicious channel."
            },
            {
              "line": 131,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Handle a role confirmed while the claimant/request remain unresolved."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "For a real Indian financial cyber-fraud loss, immediately contact bank/payment provider through a trusted route and promptly use 1930 or cybercrime.gov.in. Involve trusted adult/school safeguarding help for coercion. Preserve relevant evidence privately without delaying urgent contact. This lesson submits nothing."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Choose prompt, supportive bank/adult/official-help routes."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Build a restricted, redacted MOCK case file from supplied facts."
            },
            {
              "line": 132,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Offer help without blame, forwarding or recovery guarantees."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Synthetic same-day whole-rupee transfers only. Transparent review rule: an intermediary forwards 90â€“100% of an incoming amount within five minutes. This describes a pattern, not intent or guilt. Independent receipt RP1 explains Câ€™s group purchase; Vâ€™s source/purpose remain unresolved."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Separate observed patterns, benign context and evidence gaps."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Run the transparent rule and inspect both flagged intermediaries."
            },
            {
              "line": 133,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "State a cautious conclusion without accusing an account holder."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Prototype a verification aid, test two fictional situations and retain a before/after revision log. Pre-payment verification and after-loss help require different routes. Passing two prepared cases is limited evidence; a peer/teacher reviews usability under pressure separately."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Match safeguards to specific failure modes."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Test the weak draft, revise it and rerun both cases."
            },
            {
              "line": 134,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Handle an unanswered independent verification attempt."
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Annual capstone lesson 1 of 2: confirmed export setting, unknown download scope, unsupported AI voice claim, conflicting event amounts and an unverified beneficiary. Combine the four strands and name responsible roles; no live service or transfer changes."
            },
            {
              "line": 135,
              "kind": "Exact text",
              "text": "Build the four-strand response from separate evidence."
